.TH SPRITE 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Sprite \- A texture sliced into a grid of equal frames
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqsprite.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Sprite { Texture *tex; int frame_w, frame_h; int columns; } Sprite;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A texture sliced into a grid of equal frames. Frames are numbered left to right, top to bottom, starting at 0: frame = column + row * columns. A Sprite is a small value type: copy it freely, keep one per sheet in a scene static, and never free it (the Texture belongs to the asset cache). Build it with sprite_from().
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B tex
the sheet; NULL draws nothing
.TP
.B frame_w
width of one frame in pixels
.TP
.B frame_h
height of one frame in pixels
.TP
.B columns
frames per row, computed from the texture width by sprite_from()
.SH MODULE
sprite (src/engine/sprite/sprite.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sprite_from (3),
.BR sprite_draw (3),
.BR Anim (3),
.BR gge\-sprite (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
